    "md5": "d017251f4b48a7a4a8d761b3975f704e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1963,
    "chunk_text": "The second point I wish to bring up is this. Hon. Prime Minister, there was a circular issued providing relief to the public officers in the local government service and in local government corporations, who were deprived of employment due to the situation that prevailed in the country after July, 1983. It was primarily to do with both the Sinhala Civil Service officers working in the North and the Tamil Civil Service officers working outside the North and the East, who were affected.\n\nOne last matter I would like to raise, Hon. Prime Minister, since you are the Minister in charge of public administration. As you know, for the last week ending on 27th November, we have been commemorating the \"Great Heroes Week\" and Hon. Prime Minister, despite our differences of opinion with regard to the LTTE and politics in general, if you look at those events, you would admit that there is nothing about LTTE in those, that simply, publicly, people had been coming together to mourn their dead and that there was no LTTE paraphernalia. In fact, the police, due to some Government instructions, had approached courts right throughout the North and the East against the commemorations and except for the Court in Sampur in Trincomalee, all other courts permitted the commemoration, provided that there is no overt LTTE paraphernalia involved and a promotion of the LTTE as such. These events had been taking place over the last several years and there had been no LTTE ideology or anything of that sort being shown. There are two issues related to this: either, to the cemeteries created on government lands, the Government is refusing to allow these people to go and commemorate their dead or the military, one of the three forces, occupying private lands used as cemeteries are refusing to vacate them. They are private lands also used as cemeteries, which the Government, through the military, has subsequently been occupying and they are refusing to vacate them."
