    "chunk_index": 87,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7020055d418c5035d4694605eb1a4618",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2137,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe Constitutional Council established under the 17th Amendment, is part of the Executive and is attributed executive power.\u201d\n\nThat is for the reason that they were considering the rules which were to be made part of the Constitution for the Constitutional Council.\n\nThen, the same Determination states, I quote:\n\n\u201cThe Constitutional Council, as pointed out earlier is established by the 17th Amendment. The proposed Amendment enables the Council to exercise legislative power, \u2026\u201d\n\nWhy? Because they can make rules; it is subsidiary legislation, no doubt, and they said that it must have the approval of Parliament, but it is something of the legislative power because they can make subsidiary legislation by means of rules.\n\nNow, with regard to the Executive\u2019s power, which has been curtailed by the Constitutional Council, that must have some meaning. The Seventeenth Amendment was brought for good governance, the Determination recognizes that. It was sought to be taken away by the Eighteenth Amendment, brought back by the Nineteenth Amendment, taken away again by the Twentieth Amendment and brought back by the Twenty-first Amendment with a lot of fanfare, saying \"we are bringing this back\". But, you cannot say \"we have brought back the checks and balances on the President\" while the President behaves as though there are no checks and balances, that he is a be-all and end-all of all and that his nomination must be accepted. To say \u201cI will make only one nomination and it must be accepted\u201d is wrong. That is not the intention of Parliament when it enacted these Amendments three times over to curtail the untrammelled power of the Executive President and that must be noted because, now, we have come into a situation of another crisis of governance. This has an implication on economic recovery as well. This has also been highlighted even by the IMF. The President\n\n[\u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0daf \u0d85\u0dad \u0db4\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0daf\u0dd2 \u0d89\u0dc0\u0db8\u0d9a \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf\u0dd3.] [\u0b85\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0ba9\u0b95\u0bcd \u0b95\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0b95\u0bb3\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bbf \u0b85\u0b95\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1] [Expunged on the order of the Chair.]"
  },
