    "md5": "d36e99e6ee0a55d4f11b34e22c440e20",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2195,
    "chunk_text": "My concern is that the Hon. Sumanthiran said that I must be ashamed to be the Minister of Justice in this country. Certainly, if it came from a mediocre person, I would not be surprised or would not talk about it. But,it came from a senior President\u2019s Counsel like the Hon. Sumanthiran. It is rather shameful for you, Hon. Sumanthiran, to make a comment of that nature and you cited three examples. One is that the Magistrate of the Northern Province had issued an Order not to have rallies or protests and as a result, the police have arrested some people. You yourself know what the role of the Minister of Justice is. Has this House, by any statute, given power to the Minister of Justice to overrule a magistrate\u2019s order?\n\nAlso, on the privilege issue, Sir, I did not speak for any side. Normally, when you file a case, you do not go to the judge; parties are not allowed to have access to the judge. You first go to the registrar. Then, the registrar has to accept the plaint or the petition. After that, he has to give a number and then only he will send it to the judge. That has been the inveterate practice during the last two centuries in this country. Thereafter, of course, when the other party appears, they are entitled to take up any objection; they can even ask the notice to be recalled. In how many cases has the Hon. Sumanthiran appeared and made such applications? You know that and I also know that; we have enough experiences. But, we have to be truthful in this House.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca.\u0d92. \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca \u0d86\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd.\u0b8f. \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0bae\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd) (The Hon. M.A. Sumanthiran) On the application of the PTA, the Government has made a determination. So, why have they been arrested under the PTA?\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4 \u0d86 \u0dad\u0dd2 \u0d86\u0da5 \u0db1\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0da2\u0dba\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dc3 \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0da2\u0db4\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0ba9\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb8 \u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9c\u0baa\u0b95\u0bcd\u0bb7) (The Hon. (Dr.) Wijeyadasa Rajapakshe, PC) This is not about the determination. We were talking about this privilege issue."
  },
