    "chunk_size_bytes": 2104,
    "chunk_text": "Government. Within two years, they completely managed to destroy the trust the people had placed in that Government. The bottom line was that the institutions that were expected to take care of the people and to protect the people essentially failed. Rather, those institutions were manipulated or made to function in the interest of those in power. This is what forced the people to take to the streets; this is what forced the people to demand that those elected Representatives leave their positions. But, what is more critical is that what happened thereafter.\n\nToday, all the organs of the State are being used to justify this distorted state of affairs that is currently there in the country. We have Government Ministers who accuse each other of corruption in Parliament and who also accuse the Judiciary of being biased. The Hon. Minister of Justice himself spoke in Parliament about huge levels of corruption. Hon. Minister, I recall one instance where you spoke about the \"X-Press Pearl\" disaster. You made those statements here in Parliament, but nothing has happened. Then, former Minister of Sports and Youth made serious allegations against the Judiciary. All of that goes to erode even the minimal trust that the people have in the judicial system.\n\nThe Hon. President, [\u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0daf \u0d85\u0dad \u0db4\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0daf\u0dd2 \u0d89\u0dc0\u0db8\u0d9a \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf\u0dd3.] [\u0b85\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0ba9\u0b95\u0bcd \u0b95\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0b95\u0bb3\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bbf \u0b85\u0b95\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1] [Expunged on the order of the Chair.]\n\nas has been talked about here, has made all kinds of statements and claims, which have really damaged those institutions. For instance, take his attitude towards the Local Authorities Election, which the independent Election Commission declared. The Hon. President came to Parliament and said that he did not know what election was being talked about because no election had been declared. When the Judiciary, in a Determination, ordered that that election must take place and that the money approved by Parliament for that must be allocated, that did not happen. The Executive"
