    "chunk_text": "claims in various speeches that the people of this country do not want elections, that that is not the priority of the people, indirectly attempting to influence the Judiciary. Then, he comes to Parliament and claims that the Constitutional Council is an extension of the Executive power. He continues to make these kinds of wild and very irresponsible claims constantly, undermining the independence of the Judiciary and the role of the Judiciary in protecting the people of this country and standing by their interests.\n\nIf you look at the Bills that keep coming before us, there is a pattern where priority is given to those Bills which really seek to suppress the voice of the people and the freedoms of the people. The Prevention of Terrorism Act continues to be applied even after this very Government, some years ago, declared a moratorium on it. The Counter Terrorism Bill, which the Government put forward, was challenged, withdrawn and now, almost the same Bill is going to be presented again. Then, there is also the Online Safety Bill and several other Bills, which I do not have time to go into.\n\nWhose interest are these Bills really represent? It seems as if the main mandate of the Government in power right now is to somehow remain in power at all cost. Can there be a more dangerous situation than this? It is in this context, where this Government has demonstrated over and over again its utter and total contempt of the law, the Constitution, any kind of ethics, moral obligations, justice and of any interest in safeguarding the interests of the people and that it is willing to go to any length, that the role of the Judiciary is critical. We are rapidly approaching a point of no return, where there is potentially a complete breakdown of all we hold sacred in"
