    "chunk_size_bytes": 2079,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Presiding Member, before I begin my speech on the Votes of the Ministry of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms, I wish to take a few minutes of my allotted time to declare that I shall wear this shawl as a symbol of this House's determination to express our solidarity with the hundreds of thousands of Palestinians who are being ruthlessly subjected to the most horrifying, collective punishment on the pretext of a retaliatory war\n\n1973 1974\n\n\u0dad\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dc0 \u0dca\u200d\u0db1\u0daf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dd2\u0dbb \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0da5 (\u0d86\u0dca\u0daf\u0d9a\u0d9a] \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dca\u200d\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dca \u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0db4\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2\u0dc2 \u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dad\u0daf\n\n202] \u0dc1\u0dcf\u0dca\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0d9a 02\n\nTherefore, Sir, it is important to tell those western countries and their allies that they do not have the moral right to preach to the rest of the world about rules-based international order, the Geneva conventions and whatnot when they have deliberately encouraged and endorsed those horrible war crimes.\n\nSir, there, we are witnessing hunger or starvation as a weapon of war, denying them water and sanitation, depriving them of food, medical supplies and continuously bombarding a hapless population living in what is called the largest \"open-air prison\" in the world. If this is not genocide, what is genocide? If this is not war crimes, what in the world are war crimes is what we are asking. Therefore, we are aghast and disgusted against the double standards of the West!\n\nSir, I, therefore, solemnly say that I shall continue to wear this shawl in this House as a token of my solidarity with the Palestinian struggle, unless and until a permanent ceasefire is declared. That, Sir, is the least we could do for our brothers and sisters who are dying and being subjected to all sorts of horrible crimes in the Occupied Territories of Palestine. Long live Palestine! Also, I must thank my dear Friend, the Hon. Dilan Perera, who is in the House now and who made a similar speech yesterday in support of the struggle of the Palestinians for their liberation.\n\nI think I have a very short time left. How many minutes more do I have, Sir?"
  },
