    "chunk_text": "Then, we had a case last month where two former Presidents and a former Finance Minister had been ruled as being the people who bankrupted this country.\n\n2013 2014\n\n\u0dad\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dc0 \u0dc0 .\u0dc0 . \u0dc1\u0db4\u0daf\u0dca \u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dad\u0daf\n\n202] \u0dc1\u0dcf\u0dca\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0d9a 02\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4 \u0d86 \u0dad\u0dd2 \u0d86\u0da5 \u0db1\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0da2\u0dba\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dc3 \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0da2\u0db4\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0ba9\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9c\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb8 \u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9c\u0baa\u0b95\u0bcd\u0bb7) (The Hon. (Dr.) Wijeyadasa Rajapakshe, PC) Hon. Presiding Member, I want to respond.\n\nHon. Member, it is correct, as you said, that it is we who made the commitments and assured in January, 2015 that we would not enforce the PTA . In fact, during my tenure, it was not enforced. But, subsequently, when the Easter Sunday attack took place - I was not in the then Government - the Government in power had to make use of it since it was the law available and in fact, under the PTA, they had taken a lot of measures, not only to apprehend the culprits, but also to stop further crimes and damages from being done. Further crimes could be committed when communal issues are raised by various people, that we do not know where the end would be.\n\nAt the same time, we were dedicated and committed and through other legislations, we established the Office on Missing Persons - OMP - and the Office for Reparations. Then, the Bill to set up the Office for National Unity and Reconciliation would be presented, but it was in operation. If not for the Easter Sunday attack, whatever Government that was in power could have brought in the new Bill. That Bill had been challenged in the Supreme Court and there was a Determination and after all that clearance, it could have been passed. Anyway, due to that incident, that was hampered.\n\nLater on, when the present Government assumed responsibility in May, last year, we drafted a new Bill - of course, certain principles which had been there in the earlier Counter Terrorism Bill have also been included in that - and gazetted it. When it was gazetted, there were"
