    "md5": "52e6d737f5ce6bd964b48969f797b5d7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1895,
    "chunk_text": "Later on, when the present Government assumed responsibility in May, last year, we drafted a new Bill - of course, certain principles which had been there in the earlier Counter Terrorism Bill have also been included in that - and gazetted it. When it was gazetted, there were\n\nThen, regarding to the other incident the Hon. Member brought up - I may not be referring to the same person you mentioned - I asked from the police. Though the Hon. Member said that it was not a commemoration for the revival of the LTTE and that it had no connection with the LTTE, the police have forwarded some photographs to me. According to those, on the front side of their t-shirts, Prabhakaran\u2019s photo is there and on the back, the LTTE flag is printed. These may not be photos of the commemorations in the Eastern Province, but in the Northern Province. Hon. Member, we are trying to rebuild relations among all the communities. When some small groups, some extremists or fundamentalists, create issues like this, it is very difficult to have any reconciliation.\n\nYou know that by 2015, there were over 350 detainees under the PTA and with the assistance of the Hon. Attorney General, we released a large number of detainees. Thereafter, to hear out cases of detainees with serious charges under the PTA and conclude them, we made arrangement to establish two separate High Courts, one in Colombo and one in Anuradhapura. In fact, within a period of one and a half years or two years, they could have finished those cases very easily because there were not more than 100 cases. I also checked the progress of those courts from time to time. On most days, what had happened was that the lawyers had come and asked for future dates.\n\nTherefore, during that period they could not conclude those cases, but with all that, now it has come down to less than 20 cases altogether of convicted and remand prisoners."
