    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "e189905a11ab2da4b3861ae7c4195059",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1906,
    "chunk_text": "about. Unfortunately, we have to speak about it because we need to bring about a change, if we are going to protect the next generation. Every two hours, a child is sexually molested in this country! People may not admit it, they may not want to hear it or may not want to say it, but that is a fact and that must be accepted. One thousand seven hundred and twenty one is the number of children below the age of 16 who were raped, and that was reported in 2021. There are unreported cases, too, my fellow Members.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Minister, you have two more minutes. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dca\u0da9\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0\u0bb5\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd) (The Hon. Jeevan Thondaman) I am sure I could get more than that, Sir, as you are my friend.\n\nAnd, I would like to say that only 23 per cent - [Interruption.] Excuse me, I am speaking for the majority of the population in this country. Therefore, I think I can take some more time. I am not speaking about politics and wasting time like half the Members who spoke before me did.\n\nOnly 23 per cent of our total school strength has child protection committees. That needs to be increased; awareness needs to be created. I am sure our responsible State Minister, the Hon. (Mrs.) Geetha Samanmale Kumarasinghe, would be able to take a step forward.\n\nSir, I would also like to bring up another sensitive matter. That is, every 90 minutes, a woman is raped in Sri Lanka. These are not official statistics, but outcomes from surveys. Most women who are raped do not report it. But, we cannot use that as an excuse and say that women are not being raped."
  },
  {
