    "chunk_text": "[4.18 p.m.]\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0daf\u0db4\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) Hon. Presiding Member, I am happy to follow the Hon. State Minister of Women and Child Affairs.\n\nWe had the Indian Housing Scheme which, to a great extent, helped in alleviating that crisis. Then, of course, there have been several government schemes that were introduced. Unfortunately, those government schemes are based on providing funds for the building of houses, which are grossly inadequate and are released in stages. So, what happenes is, for the first stage, a certain sum is released and you are supposed to construct the house to a certain limit and it is only after that, the second tranche of funds would get released. But, when the amount of money that is released in the first instance is inadequate - more often than not, it has been grossly inadequate - then,\n\n2207 2208\n\n\u0db4\u0daf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dc0\n\nobviously, to proceed with that housing project, people struggle. So, what has happened over time, especially, in the case of those women-headed households, is that they are forced to take a loan to complete that first stage in order to get the second stage of funds to be released from the Government and by doing that, they get into a rut, they get into a vicious debt cycle."
  },
