    "chunk_text": "Without calling for any interviews - they cannot just do that because these are not permanent cadres - they had simply taken them in and therefore, there is a serious injustice caused to others. There are several other teachers who had already applied. What happens to them? They have lost their opportunity to get in there. These people have been attached for that particular purpose for a short period of time. This preferential treatment by certain people there, is causing a serious problem and I hope, since the Minister is aware of what is happening there, he will look into this matter.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0daf, \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0daf\u0da7 \u0dc1\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc5 \u0daf\u0dbd\u0d9a \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\u0dca\u0daf \u0dba\u0dd2. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0db1 \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf \u0bb1\u0bb5\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Okay, Sir. Yesterday, the Hon. (Dr.) Wijeyadasa Rajapakshe had taken up a matter regarding which I have certain comments to make. Since my time is up, I will speak about it tomorrow. I think the Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam also will raise a Privilege issue tomorrow since his name also had been dragged in for a different issue. But, I would like to talk about another Member\u2019s comments on judges. I think we will have to correctly apply our Privileges because the procedure should not be abused. Privileges should be there, but under the guise of trying to exercise the Privilege of free speech, you cannot go on using outrageously intemperate accusations and wordings. So, these have to be avoided. I will deal with it when that Privilege issue is taken up by the Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam tomorrow morning. In fact, I mentioned to the Hon. Speaker today at the meeting of the Committee of Selection that I have serious reservations about what happened in the House the other day.\n\nThank you.\n\n2409 2410\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0da5 \u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0dae \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0daf]\n\n2023 \u0dc1\u0dcf\u0dca\u0dd0 \u0db6\u0d9a 05"
