    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "d67565034618fbd373ff5873ba3ab995",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1473,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Presiding Member, firstly, I would like to congratulate the Hon. Minister Susil Premajayantha and his team of State Ministers for giving priority to the concept of English education. I am someone who had had the good fortune of being educated in English. I know its advantages and sincerely hope that that advantage or that practice is available to everybody.\n\nThen, with regard to the situation of education in the North and the East, especially in the backdrop where the Provincial Councils are not functioning, unfortunately, a Cabinet Minister who had been elected from Jaffna has taken it upon himself to use the Ministry of Education in the Provincial Council as a private property. He, as a result, has been interfering in all the transfers, which ideally ought to have been taking place through the Transfer Board that, under Circular No. 2007/20, includes unions and heads of departments.\n\nThat is a circular applicable to all the provincial councils right throughout the country. But, in transfers in the North, in particular, and in the East as well, that\n\n2439 2440\n\n\u0db4\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dc1 \u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\n\nCabinet Minister who had been elected from Jaffna uses his influence and intervenes and as a result, it is just throwing the whole system out of sync. Therefore, I appeal to the Minister, the Hon. Susil Premajayantha, to intervene in this matter and make sure that such interferences do not take place. It must be looked into as a matter of priority."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
