    "chunk_index": 231,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "d0af0d792d4e483f41c0819474533fda",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1965,
    "chunk_text": "Cabinet Minister who had been elected from Jaffna uses his influence and intervenes and as a result, it is just throwing the whole system out of sync. Therefore, I appeal to the Minister, the Hon. Susil Premajayantha, to intervene in this matter and make sure that such interferences do not take place. It must be looked into as a matter of priority.\n\nThen, with regard to the situation in universities, the State university system, quite honestly in my opinion, is going into a crisis. There is a brain drain. People are wanting to leave the country because of its economic situation. This will definitely threaten to paralyze education activities. The academics, the non-academic staff and the technical staff are either permanently leaving the country or taking advantage of the opportunity to go on no-pay leave. Some who go on leave are exploring the possibility of finding permanent jobs overseas and may not even return. That is a grave danger happening, not only in the higher education field, but also in other sectors, particularly in the health sector, and I think the Hon. Minister concerned must address that situation.\n\nAnother reason why this brain drain is taking place is, the way in which taxation is handled. University teachers have been affected by the new tax regime. The Federation of University Teachers Association - FUTA - has submitted some reforms to the current tax regime. Amendments are needed to that, Hon. State Minister. The Government has to seriously take into consideration an individual's ability to pay taxes. A blanket system that applies uniformly to everyone is unfair. Factors such as the number of dependents of the individual, the previous loans he has obtained et cetera should be taken into consideration in that. The introduction of a wealth tax and the taxation of big businesses, I think, should be the way out, not so much the current approach. So, I think that is another reason which is causing this brain drain."
  },
