    "chunk_text": "And also, Hon. Minister, the probationary lecturers have to sign a bond, if they want to go on study leave to pursue postgraduate programmes overseas. That amount of the bond is huge and that is mainly because the Government is factoring the scholarship money provided by western universities and scholarship-warding institutions such as the Fulbright Commission in calculating the bond amount. Due to the depreciation of the rupee, that figure has risen exponentially. Probationary lecturers are unable to find guarantors. Young academics with a commitment to serve the country are sadly resigning from their positions. This also discourages young academics from pursuing their higher studies in internationally acclaimed universities overseas. Therefore, the system which factors in scholarship money and other stipends provided by overseas institutions should be abolished.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Member, please wind up. Your time is over.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0daf\u0db4\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) I am winding up, Sir. I table* that letter written by the Arts Faculty Students' Union.\n\nThere are huge disparities between the University of Colombo and the universities outside, especially those in the North and the East, when it comes to allocation of human resources in certain disciplines or areas. I would like to point out the sociology statistics which appeared in a UGC publication released in 2022. If the State cannot create new cadre positions, it should actively redistribute the existent cadres in such a way that the universities in the North and the East and outside Colombo could also remain academically vibrant."
  },
