    "chunk_text": "There are huge disparities between the University of Colombo and the universities outside, especially those in the North and the East, when it comes to allocation of human resources in certain disciplines or areas. I would like to point out the sociology statistics which appeared in a UGC publication released in 2022. If the State cannot create new cadre positions, it should actively redistribute the existent cadres in such a way that the universities in the North and the East and outside Colombo could also remain academically vibrant.\n\n2441 2442\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0db4\u0daf\u0db1\u0dca \u0db6\u0dbd \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0daf]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0dc4\u0dd4\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0daf \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bae\u0bb2\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\n2023 \u0dc1\u0dcf\u0dca\u0dd0 \u0db6\u0d9a 05\n\ncomplete opposite is happening; it is a very unhealthy position. I believe that if we are to progress, students must be given - it is lawful - within democratic limits the opportunity to freely engage in political thought and in political activity to a point that it will create a society that is more representative as opposed to something that is prescriptive.\n\nThank you.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0dab\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0d9d\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b95\u0bb5\u0ba9\u0bcd) (The Hon. (Dr.) Suren Raghavan) Sir, I will take 30 seconds to respond to the Hon. Ponnambalam. I think he raised many pertinent issues, on which we find common ground. His last point that militarization is taking place in higher education centres in the Northern Province is somewhat contested and I would say that recent incidents show contradiction."
