    "md5": "43f96d1b9beb7d88e5d2bda297fccab0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1882,
    "chunk_text": "Having said that and expressed solidarity to the Palestinian people, let me now engage in the Discussion on the Votes of the Ministry of Education, which is led by the Hon. (Dr.) Susil Premajayantha. Alongside him, we have the State Minister of Education, the Hon. A. Aravindh Kumar, and the State Minister of Higher Education, the Hon. (Dr.) Suren Raghavan, akin to Hon. Minister\u2019s right and left hands, providing valuable support and strength to enhance the education system.\n\nIn the meantime, let me draw your attention to the many shortcomings prevailing in the Batticaloa Central Education Zone. Hon. Aravindh Kumar, you must be knowing that the Batticaloa Central Education Zone stands out for its achievements in both the academic and sports domains, earning numerous national awards and recognition. The operational hub of the Batticaloa Central Education Zone is currently situated in the premises of Al-Juffriya Vidyalaya in Eravur Town, but it has been facing challenges due to insufficient space and basic amenities since inception. Therefore, I respectfully urge the Hon. Minister to promptly support the establishment of a fully-equipped zonal office complete with necessary furniture and equipment.\n\nThere are numerous schools in the Batticaloa Central Education Zone which have secured multiple victories at national and provincial competitions. Nevertheless, it is worth highlighting that those schools, currently, lack sufficient sports and recreation facilities. Hence, there is a crucial need for the development and provision of sports grounds as well as recreational facilities and equipment for those institutions.\n\nFurther, deficiency in furniture affects both students and teachers in a majority of schools. These schools continue to rely on furniture provided more than 10 to 15\n\nyears ago, which need reparation, but no funds are allocated for the same."
  },
