    "chunk_size_bytes": 1872,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, I am glad that it is the Hon. State Minister of Foreign Affairs who will be responding to this Motion along with the Hon. Minister of Public Security because my view is that the Cabinet Minister of Foreign Affairs is not fit to hold that portfolio, considering the fact that he had been the personal counsel of somebody who is accused of crimes against humanity and also economic crimes. So, I am glad that the Cabinet Minister in charge of foreign affairs is not responding and that it is the State Minister who would, since the Cabinet Minister\u2019s opinion does not really count as there is a conflict of interest.\n\nRight now, the number of people who are migrating or leaving this country and seeking asylum in foreign countries has increased. That is because they cannot live within this country. They are arrested under the PTA for memorialization of their dead. There were no LTTE flags or symbols relating to the LTTE at those events in Batticaloa, but they were arrested. There was a young boy who is 18 years old and a school student. The only thing he did was, he accompanied his father, who provided equipment for that event. He also had been arrested and detained. His school has given a letter regarding his studentship. Then, a person who works in a bakery had been arrested for selling a cake! Now, how do you expect the Tamils to live in this country and expect us to believe that the Government is genuine in its reconciliation efforts? Livestock farmers are forced to sell their cattle because you are taking over their pasture land; you all are not letting them live.\n\nThere is intimidation from the TID and the CID. Apart from the membersof the Government parties, the others connected to the Ilankai Tamil Arausu Kadchi and other political parties from the North and the East are being intimidated, even today. They do not even want us\n\n2491 2492"
