    "chunk_text": "What happened over the last week with regard to those commemorative events is important, Sir, because the Government\u2019s stated policy from the President down is that commemorations are allowed, and it has been repeatedly stated. Thereafter, the police went to the\n\n2493 2494\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc2\u0daf\u0dab\u0dca\u200d\u0dca\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0d9a\u0db1\u0dca \u0daf\u0da2\u0db4\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dbb \u0db1\u0dca \u0daf\u0dca\u0db8\u0daf\u0dab\u0dd2\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0daf]\n\n2023 \u0dc1\u0dcf\u0dca\u0dd0 \u0db6\u0d9a 05\n\nBut, instead, what happened was the complete opposite: people were prevented from commemorating their dead. In fact, the Batticaloa Organizer of our alliance, the Tamil National People\u2019s Front, went to one of the cemeteries with his son. Had hired a vehicle to take some red and yellow flags, simply red and yellow flags, to the cemetery and when he went, he was turned back. The police refused to allow him and other people there to commemorate. So, he turned back; he did not even commemorate. He turned back, was on his way to the Batticaloa Town and midway through, was stopped at another checkpoint and there, the police decided to arrest the vehicle and the driver. Why? Because, they had red and yellow flags. Red and yellow are the colours of Tamil nationalism. My party is the All Ceylon Tamil Congress. In our flag, we have red and yellow; the Federal Party also has red and yellow. Long superseding the LTTE or any militant groups, that war criminal Pillaiyan had had red and yellow in his flag. But, for having red and yellow flags, they were taken into custody. My organizer and his son went along with the police - they were not even arrested, they went along because it was my organizer who hired that vehicle - and at the time of 6.05 p.m., the son of our organizer wanted to commemorate and asked the police and the police said, \u201cGo outside and light a lamp\u201d. When he did it, he was then arrested. All of them were arrested under the PTA."
