    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "d54478a6c0e31d6e395c83ad84a2a847",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1785,
    "chunk_text": "So, what I say is, do not focus on a particular race. We all are Sri Lankans; whether we are Tamils, Sinhalese or Muslims, we all are Sri Lankans. We have to just get together and work towards protecting human rights. That is our duty. My Fellow Members who moved and seconded the Motion are well-educated politicians. I think you all have broader minds. Just stop being racist and work as Sri Lankans. So, I urge the well-educated Members of this House, please, let us work together, just forget about the past and move forward. Thank you.\n\n[7.09 p.m.]\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0dc3 \u0dba\u0dd2\u0da9\u0dca \u0d85\u0dbd\u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b9a\u0baf\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb2\u0bbf \u0bb8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb9\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bc8\u0bcc\u0bb2\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bc6\u0bbe) (The Hon. Seyed Ali Zahir Moulana) Hon. Deputy Speaker, I stand before you with concerns about the abuse of the Prevention of Terrorism Act of Sri Lanka, particularly against the youth who wanted to talk about their rights or who were commemorating those who had fought for their rights.\n\nThe PTA has been used to justify numerous human rights violations including torture, sexual abuse, arbitrary detention and violation of international law. Members of all communities in Sri Lanka have suffered consistent discrimination and harassment, especially the Muslim community from 2013, culminating in the adoption of Government policies explicitly targeting the majority group.\n\nThe PTA has been expanded to include crimes such as property damage, theft and robbery and restrict the rights to freedom of assembly and speech. This vague and overbroad legislation has led to serious human rights violations as seen in the case of protestors, minority groups and political opponents, with them being targeted by the Government."
  },
