    "chunk_text": "When Hon. Ranil Wickremesinghe became the President, he not only spoke of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission and the Office for Overseas Sri Lankan Affairs which he started, but he expedited the\n\nI regret that a certain narrative is being built. Pertaining to the PTA, in 2017, the previous Government -the Yahapalana Government- gave an assurance that the PTA will be amended and in March 2022. The PTA was amended after 43 years. As a result of that amendment, so many Tamil prisoners who were in prison for a very long period of time were released.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dba \u0db1\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0da2\u0dba \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dd2, \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0daf\u0da7 \u0dad\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d \u0dc3\u0dd2 \u0daf\u0da9\u0dd2\u0d9a \u0daf\u0dbd\u0d9a\u0dca \u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dc1\u0db6 \u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\u0daf.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dad\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0db6\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dba \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95 \u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0b9a\u0bc2\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baf) (The Hon. Tharaka Balasuriya) And we have also given a commitment to the international community that the PTA will be repealed and a new anti-terrorism law will be brought forward. The Cabinet Subcommittee was appointed in September 2022 and on 20th February 2023, the Cabinet approved the Bill but there was a lot of feedback from the Bar Association and civil society, which said that they need to do further deliberations and on the 28th of August 2023, the Cabinet approval was given for the Bill. On the 1st of September 2023, a diplomatic briefing was conveyed in the Ministry of Foreign Affairs explaining about the new Bill.\n\nI am sure, there are shortcomings and I am sure that we cannot satisfy everyone with regard to this Bill; but I think we need to stop building this narrative in which you are saying that the Government is trying to suppress the Tamils and because of that, the Tamils are leaving the country. If you look, Hon. Deputy Speaker, even the Sinhalese are leaving the country. That is because of the economic condition in the country - [Interruption] Yes. So, there are other reasons why people are leaving. You are not talking about that but you are only talking about one aspect of that."
